# Phone app environment. Copy to apps/mobile/.env for local dev. EAS builds take
# their values from the build profile in eas.json (and EAS environment
# variables), not from this file.
#
# Every EXPO_PUBLIC_ value is baked into the bundle: restart Metro with a clean
# cache (`npx expo start -c`) after changing one, and never put a secret here.
#
# The phone app doesn't use NODE_ENV. Its equivalent is React Native's __DEV__,
# true only in a development build served by Metro (docs/environments.md).

# --- Where the API and Storage are ---------------------------------------------
# A phone is not your laptop: `localhost` resolves to the phone itself. Leave
# these two out and a development build uses the address Metro is served from,
# so it follows you between networks. `npm run mobile:tunnel` sets them to its
# tunnel URLs. A preview or production build must have both, or it throws at
# launch.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:3001
# Only used to rewrite signed file links so a phone can reach local Storage.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:54321

# [optional] development | staging | production. Only tags Sentry reports. EAS
# builds set it per profile in eas.json (development, preview → staging,
# production); leave it unset for local dev.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

# --- Error reporting (docs/error-handling.md) ----------------------------------
# [optional] Sentry DSN. Unset = no error reporting. Needs a build made after
# the @sentry/react-native plugin was added (Oct 2026).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# --- Subscriptions (docs/billing.md) -------------------------------------------
# [optional] RevenueCat public SDK keys, one per platform. Unset hides buying.
# Until the stores are connected, a RevenueCat Test Store key (test_...) in both
# works on either platform. Needs a development build made after
# react-native-purchases was added (Oct 2026).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=
